# TypeScript Standards

## Configuration

Strict mode enabled (`tsconfig.json`). Path alias: `@/*` → `src/*`.

## Typing Rules

- **Never use `any`** unless absolutely unavoidable — prefer `unknown` + type guards
- Define domain types near their usage (see `farm-store.ts`: `Garden`, `ActivityLog`)
- Use Supabase generated types from `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
- Map DB snake_case to app camelCase in mapper functions

```typescript
// Good: explicit types
type GardenRow = { id: string; name: string; planted_at: string; ... };
const mapGarden = (r: GardenRow): Garden => ({ ... });

// Good: Zod validation for server function inputs
const Input = z.object({ mode: z.enum(["farm", "expert"]), ... });
```

## Server Functions

```typescript
export const myFunction = createServerFn({ method: "POST" })
  .middleware([requireSupabaseAuth])  // if auth needed
  .inputValidator((d: unknown) => InputSchema.parse(d))
  .handler(async ({ data, context }) => { ... });
```

## Imports

- Use `@/` path alias for src imports
- Type-only imports when appropriate: `import type { ... }`
- Do not import from `server-only` package (TanStack Start uses different convention)

## Enums & Constants

Activity types are string union types, not TS enums:

```typescript
export type ActivityType = "Tưới nước" | "Bón phân" | ...;
export const ACTIVITY_TYPES: ActivityType[] = [...];
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
catch (e) {
  toast.error(e instanceof Error ? e.message : "Có lỗi xảy ra");
}
```

Always narrow errors — never assume `Error` type.
